data/hashing/siphash/

vectors.h is an unmodified copy of the file of that name in the reference
implementation of SipHash by Jean-Philippe Aumasson and Daniel J. Bernstein,
https://github.com/veorq/SipHash, at commit
32d067603b93b47828700880649198e0bfbbcffa, downloaded on 2026-10-25, SHA-256
212c44114a63c6d84710b8627f3bc5ce155698accf2ea7bbff1c4b69c9f48d31.  The
repository offers its files under CC0 1.0, the MIT license, or the Apache
License 2.0 with LLVM exceptions.  Its array vectors_sip64 gives the eight tag
bytes of SipHash-2-4, least significant first, for the key 00 01 ... 0f and
the messages 00 01 ... (i - 1) for i from 0 to 63, as the repository's test.c
computes them.

vectors.txt holds SipHash-2-4 and SipHash-1-3 tags that generate.py wrote on
2026-10-25 with the SIPHASH MAC of OpenSSL 3.5.4, whose parameters c-rounds
and d-rounds select the variant.  Each line gives a pseudorandom 16-byte key,
the two tags as the sixteen hexadecimal digits of their 64-bit values, and a
pseudorandom message from Python's random.Random(2012): one message of every
length from 0 to 256 bytes and of the lengths 511, 512, 513, 1000, 1023, 1024,
1025, 4095, 4096, and 4097.  generate.py checks OpenSSL against the 64 vectors
of vectors.h and against the test value 0xa129ca6149be45e5 of Appendix A of
the SipHash paper, https://cr.yp.to/siphash/siphash-20120918.pdf, before it
writes the file.
